From da0fd7af290a15eeec984ba60f7a87e99d9ebfe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 09:10:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(render): block network access, substitute template
 slots in one pass, wrap long header values

- Chrome now cannot reach the network (DNS blocked, all requests sent to a dead proxy,
  loopback included); verified with a local server that is hit without the flags.
- build_html replaced slots one after another, so a customer name such as {{CLOSING}}
  was replaced by the letter text; it is now a single pass over the template.
- Very long unbreakable names wrap instead of overflowing and failing verification.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SvuRq1Eofn4b6USYJT5xnT
---
